  "Number": 10,
  "Question": "A picture \\(3\\) feet across is hung in the center of a wall that is \\(19\\) feet wide. How many feet from the end of the wall is the nearest edge of the picture?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(1\\dfrac12\\)",
    "B": "\\(8\\)",
    "C": "\\(9\\dfrac12\\)",
    "D": "\\(16\\)",
    "E": "\\(22\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Because the picture is centered, the empty spaces on its left and right have equal widths. Together these spaces measure\n\\[\n19-3=16\\text{ feet}.\n\\]\nEach space is half of that total:\n\\[\n16\\div2=8\\text{ feet}.\n\\]\nThe nearest edge of the picture is \\(8\\) feet from either end of the wall, choice \\(\\mathrm{B}\\).",
